Hello. I've performed RSWAT simulations using the RStudio version without the GUI interface, following your advice. However, I'm encountering issues during the water quality modeling process. Currently, I'm working on optimizing model parameters for 9 monitoring points. The problem I'm facing is that the observation time steps for each point are not consistent. In the example file I've attached, there are observations for 1 point related to flow and 2 points related to water quality.

My specific issue arises when executing the code:

behavioral <- behaSimulation(obj$objValueCali,
                             obj$simData,
                             parameterValue,
                             behThreshold,
                             varNumber,
                             objFunction,
                             observedData,
                             minOrmax,
                             samplingApproach)

I'm receiving an "out of bound" error during this process. I would greatly appreciate your advice on how to resolve this problem. Thank you.

